<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What RFID formats does Hana manufacture?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Dry and wet RFID inlays on reel, and ruggedized UHF tags, including tags embedded in tires. Cards and other finished formats are covered on the RFID market pages.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What is the difference between a dry and a wet inlay?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">A dry inlay consists of the RFID chip and antenna on its substrate. A wet inlay adds an adhesive layer so it can be applied directly during converting. Hana manufactures both formats.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What makes a tire tag different from a standard RFID tag?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">A tire tag is embedded in rubber during vulcanization, so it must withstand cure temperatures and then repeated flexing during service. The antenna, chip attach and encapsulation materials are selected for this environment.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What frequencies and chips do you support?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">HF and UHF constructions, with the antenna matched to the chip and application. Tire tags are UHF to ISO 18000-63 / EPC Gen 2. Hana is IC independent and works with Impinj, NXP, ASYGN, Oxzon and other suppliers.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Are inlays and tags tested before shipping?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Every unit is encoded and read-verified before shipment, with per-unit traceability. Inlays on reel include bad-mark handling.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What quality systems cover RFID production?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">ISO 9001 applies group-wide and IATF 16949 applies to automotive work. Production runs in ESD-controlled areas meeting ANSI/ESD S20.20, and the Ohio site is ARC-certified for RFID inlay design and manufacturing.</div>
    </details>
